2. **SCST CAW abort-reclaim fix** (your other session's work) — deployed and **live** at `3.11.0-pre+caw-abort-reclaim.1`. Had to clear a live D-state wedge first (via `scst_unwedge.ko`, no host reboot) and rebuild `iscsi-scst` to match the version string. The first 16-node run hit the exact wedge it fixes — so it's load-bearing for reliable testing.

**The breakthrough (from scaling down to 2 nodes):** `posix_multi16`'s blocker is **not** 16-node contention/slowness — it's a **correctness bug in `test_dir_stress` that reproduces at 2 nodes in ~8s.** It's **asymmetric**: node1 (the parent-dir owner) fails to see *any* of node2's 20 dirs, while node2 sees node1's fine. The shared parent dir grows to block/btree format and the owner's cached dir-data blocks aren't reloaded on the peer's modify — block-format-dir read staleness. P78 did not fix this (different failure mode). This passes `cache_coherency` (4-node) only because that uses small/shortform dirs.

**Corrections I owe you:** parallel reboots don't scale with node count (I was wrong); some of my verification loops were serial (fixing). And my "slow at 2 nodes" read was wrong — the run was progressing; I'd just cut it off.

